    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7242" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">căvĕātus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		id. (Plinian). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>Encaged</i>, <i>cooped up</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 6,
				5, § 13</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> (Acc. to cavea, II D.) <i>Arranged
				like the</i> cavea <i>in a theatre</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 8, 15, § 30</span></i>
			.</div>
